1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
ENKI’s private iOS app, authentication and glasses camera
existed before this hackathon.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The new work is Second Memory: bounded observation, Meta visual
analysis, evidence storage and recall.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The question is simple: where did I last see my keys? The answer
must point to evidence, not a guess.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The session requires iOS authorization and consent. Observation
is visible and limited to five minutes.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Sampling is automatic within the active foreground session,
capped at one selected image per second.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Sampling does not mean automatic upload or permanent memory.
Those actions require separate consent.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
For this controlled test, the scene contains test keys on a
table, with no personal or third-party content.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
One manual analysis sends one authorized image through an HTTPS
backend. The API key stays on the server.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Muse Spark 1.3 returns a structured scene and objects. We
display uncertainty and provider provenance.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
We inspect the actual image and result before deciding whether
to save this observation locally.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Saving is explicit. The record links capture time, analysis and
the exact image used as evidence.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
After stopping observation, we ask where the keys were last
seen. Retrieval reads saved records only.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The result shows the latest matching capture time and its image.
It does not claim the keys are still there.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:20,000
This version uses a basic text query for keys. It does not
provide wake-word listening or general conversation.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Individual deletion needs confirmation. Locking or leaving the
foreground stops the protected workflow.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The independent package runs without private ENKI. Its offline
tests and synthetic demo are labelled clearly.

17
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Second Memory is a prototype of evidence-linked recall, with
explicit privacy controls and honest limits.
